{
 "about": "remote_view.neutral(text, limit) after the fix: one short line of text an agent or a connector supplied (a connector's name, a health check's unknown detail, an agent's plan, a tool's title): control characters gone, credentials masked, `[`/`]` as `(`/`)`, `<`/`>` as look-alikes, a zero-width space after the colon of every `://` and the `www` of every `www.`, escaped ones too (the chat's rich text and a client link a bare address by themselves), clipped to `limit`. Generated from the Python worker; the TypeScript port must give the same. A bare domain (the answer's rule) gets a zero-width space before the dot of its last label, and a mail address one right after its `@`.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "about": "connector name",
   "input": "dev-pod https://evil.example/x",
   "limit": 200,
   "expected": "dev-pod https:​//evil.example/x"
  },
  {
   "about": "health detail",
   "input": "see https://evil.example/fix for details",
   "limit": 200,
   "expected": "see https:​//evil.example/fix for details"
  },
  {
   "about": "plan text",
